From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] kiln: Reboot and Shutdown through Kiln's update agent, touch
 units tag

Kiln OS (after v1.0.0-rc2) routes Moonraker's machine.reboot and
machine.shutdown through its root update agent, which refuses while a
print may run, while the recovery OS is being written into slot A, and
for the first 10 minutes after boot while start-up has not finished.
The screen's own Reboot and Shutdown skipped all of that: on a host
without systemd it ran /sbin/reboot or /sbin/poweroff itself, as root,
and after any failed RPC it fell back to them.

- On HELIX_KILN_AD5X builds (helix::kiln_host_power()) the shutdown
  dialog always goes through Moonraker (ShutdownDialogMode
  KilnViaMoonraker, plan_power_dialog): no local power-off, whatever the
  connection or the error. A refusal closes the dialog and a toast says
  why ("Can't restart the printer: A print is running"); without a
  connection, "Not connected to the printer".
- The home Shutdown tile and Advanced's Shutdown and Reboot rows are
  greyed while a job holds the machine (kiln_power_locked, from
  job_holds_machine, published after PrinterState's subjects), as Boot
  into recovery is greyed during a print.
- Touch calibration: every save of the touch range writes
  input.ad5x_touch_units, "stock" on the 5.10 kernel and "own" on Kiln's
  kernels. Kiln's ad5x-touch-units takes a range without the tag for
  stock units, so a calibration made on Kiln's kernel after a factory
  reset was converted a second time and touch was off.

Other builds keep upstream's behaviour. Strings in en and ru.

Tests: the Kiln plan for every host and connection, other builds'
plan unchanged, the refusal texts (with and without the reason in
front), the lock following job_holds_machine only on Kiln, the units by
kernel release and the tag written on Kiln saves only.

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
