+/**
+ * Kiln OS: Reboot and Shutdown through Moonraker only.
+ *
+ * Kiln's Moonraker hands machine.reboot and machine.shutdown to its root
+ * update agent, which refuses while a print may run, while the recovery OS is
+ * being written and before start-up has finished. On Kiln builds the dialog
+ * therefore always goes through Moonraker (never the local /sbin/reboot or
+ * /sbin/poweroff, which would skip those checks), and a refusal is shown with
+ * its reason, and the power entries are greyed while a job holds the machine
+ * (kiln_power_locked). Other builds keep upstream's plan.
+ */
